# The Lighthouse

The keeper climbed the stairs at dusk. Every night he counted them: one
hundred and twelve, never more, never less. The lamp waited at the top.

## The Storm

Rain came from the west. The sea rose against the rocks, and the old
tower shook! Would the light hold until morning? He trusted it would.

## Morning

At dawn the water was calm again. The keeper wrote one line in the log:
"The light held." Then he slept.
